cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or discuss this work, please cite the repository and the version you consulted."
type: software
title: "grAIph: Graph-Structured Infrastructure for LLM Software Generation"
abstract: >
  grAIph is a research system for representing software-generation architecture
  as an explicit graph. The graph is compiled into topological generation order,
  context representations, contracts, validation stages, and evidence-aware
  reconciliation. The public repository documents the architecture, hypotheses,
  benchmark protocol, and current evidence boundaries; the implementation remains
  private while the system is being hardened.
